comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-20T17:35:05.757Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence 2026-08-20: dependency add and remove now share the same malformed shorthand validator. A removal selector matching zero rows fails with dependency_remove_no_match, exit 3, unmatched selectors, the compact available dependency identities, and recovery steps; malformed unprefixed comma values fail with dependency_flag_value_invalid, exit 2, flag and value context. CLI JSON classification and generated error contracts preserve those typed fields. A temporary end-to-end tracker confirmed both failures and confirmed valid selective removal. Linked update tests passed 107/107, mutation integrity tests brought the combined run to 110/110, and structured CLI guidance passed 45/45."
  "2026-08-20T17:37:45.540Z","harness:codex","Repository-wide verification 2026-08-20: pnpm test:coverage passed 539 files and 7,644 tests at exact 100% statements, branches, functions, and lines; pnpm quality:static passed generated contracts, SDK surface, package parity, grammar, token budgets, tracker context, graph composition, record integrity, and transport floors; ESLint passed with zero warnings; jscpd found zero clones across 1,067 files; docs links passed; secret scan found no credential-like material; pnpm audit found no known vulnerabilities. Manual acceptance used a disposable initialized tracker and verified semantic traversal, duplicate collapse without edge absence, malformed removal refusal, and typed zero-match recovery."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-20T17:35:06.378Z","harness:codex","Mutation success must mean a state transition. Shared grammar plus typed zero-match context lets SDK, CLI, and MCP callers recover without rereading the full item or trusting a silent no-op."
